From bceb6084eb082d5856d48e55a065f7df78cc94f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:59:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Our own photo resizer, photos full screen, Full map,
 commercial property in the analyzer

Photos: the copy is now made smaller by our own resizer (idx-lib/shrink.js with jpeg-js, vendored
in idx-lib/vendor, no add-on to install): a card photo goes from about 750 KB to about 45 KB, a
listing-page photo to about 250 KB, once per photo per 30 days. Cloudflare's paid resizing is not
used. If a copy ever fails, the page loads the photo from the MLS at once.

Listing page, signed up: a click on any photo, or on "All photos", opens the photos full screen;
arrows, a swipe or the keyboard page through them, with "3 of 33".

Map: the map is its own layer, so the 2D and 3D buttons always sit above it; a Full map button
puts the list aside and fills the screen (full screen where the browser allows), and brings it
back.

Analyzer: the booking popup never opens while it works or shows its numbers. A "Kind of property"
choice (a home, office, retail store, warehouse or industrial, restaurant, other business), set
from the MLS type when the listing has one: a commercial property is figured by rent per square
foot a year and its usual lease (NNN, modified gross or gross), with commercial vacancy, value
from income and commercial sales, and flags on lease, zoning, parking, access, building systems
and environmental risk. No home comparisons or home-area targets are shown for it.

